{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The Breeze felt like a natural next choice after Old Sock because I wanted another relaxed blues listen.",
    "Different Shades Of Blue and Gary Clark Jr. Live fit the guitar-driven blues interest reflected in my listening to Memphis and People, Hell & Angels."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25 missed what I wanted today because contemporary pop ballads do not offer the blues-oriented listening I was seeking.",
    "Croz, New and Blood On The Tracks have appealing songwriting or established musicians, but those connections were less compelling than the blues sound I wanted this visit."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Interest in established rock musicians seemed to count too broadly; a familiar musician alone does not make an album my next choice.",
    "My listening to Blown Away did not mean I wanted other contemporary vocal releases such as 25 right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The connection to Old Sock mattered especially strongly today: I wanted a relaxed blues album, which made The Breeze stand out.",
    "An album can fit my taste without being something I would choose now; I would save several appealing blues and roots records for later rather than keep selecting albums this visit."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my blues and guitar interests, but some stretched that interest into broader rock and pop choices that were less relevant to this visit."
}"}
